spec-1 / runtime-1 (docs/research/deepinfer/spec-decode.md, runtime.md): opt Qwen GDN into
vLLM 0.31's adaptive verification, mirroring the KDA opt-in of vllm#52988 (88aa0d287d).
Experimental, against the image's installed (already patched) vLLM. Inert unless the env
knobs are set; single-user/start_qwen.sh ADAPTIVE_VERIFY=1 sets both.

VLLM_GDN_ADAPTIVE_VERIFY=1 (gdn_attn.py):
- GDNAttentionBackend.supports_device_cpu_query_lens_mismatch() -> True.
- GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder.get_varlen_cudagraph_max_query_len() -> num_spec + 1
  (kept UNIFORM_BATCH instead of KDA's ALWAYS: prefill batches still never replay a
  FULL graph, only the varlen decode check is satisfied).
- spec_sequence_masks_cpu &= query_len <= num_spec + 1 (profiler dummy rows).
- uniform_spec_sequence_length left None (the CPU split is a placeholder).
VLLM_FA2_VARLEN_VERIFY=1 (flash_attn.py): FA2 (UNIFORM_BATCH, no bound upstream) reports
a varlen bound of k+1 so the FLASH_ATTN target (CTX=fast, FA2_FP8KV plugin) passes the
same boot check. Whether FA2 / the fp8 plugin really honour device q_len < host bound is
exactly what the greedy bit-identity run decides.

